      "side": 1,
      "message": "Once you make the change at line 292, I think you\u0027ll find that this code is implicitly using |this|.\n\nI believe that will work ok, since we\u0027ve acquired the sp at line 293. Stylistically, though, this makes the code a bit subtle. For clarity, I\u0027d rather we only access the object only through |shared_ptr|.\n\nThat will probably require either exposing a public method to access event_callbacks_, or a public method to invoke onBackgroundScanFailure() on all event listeners.\n\nBut avoiding implicit use of |this| still seems like the right thing to do, given that the lambda might outlive the object.",
